/-!
# The doubled branch of source 11.3.6

The leaves prove the E.6.1 setup and E-generation for the actual doubled
module and construct its F.7.6 setup on N_M(C_T(V_M)). Under weak-closure
containment, F.7.11 supplies a noncommuting doubled conjugate in the original T.
Its actual fixed-space-family image lies in the natural SL₃ component.
Both centralizer coranks are 2n, both full plane-shear actions are constructed,
and the intersection equals the commutator of order 2^(4n).
Both actions preserve the original natural constituents and have the same
kernels on those constituents as on the full modules. The original seed commutator has order 2^n and is a field line on both sides.
Alignment with the supplied source flag and 11.3.4(4) excludes this pair,
proving weak-closure escape and giving k=2n under the preceding upper bound.
The local involution minimum and global s-value are proved to equal 2n on
the original full module, and the literal automizer has two-rank at most 3n.
The leaves also prove its selected Sylow image and
fixed-space uniformity, the reciprocal
rank budget, and the G.1.6 application at degree 2n with multiplicity one.
Reciprocal plane shears give the maximal Sylow commutator dimension and
equal nonzero individual commutator planes. They construct orthogonal
coordinates on the moving part of the original omega orbit, allowing a fixed
summand, and contradict its literal source action. The source consumer keeps
the original D, S, H and star projection. The reciprocal shear coordinates are now constructed from the original doubled
marking and the two literal centralizer indices. The pointwise-centralizer argument now proves r>2n, constructs the full original
Geometry, and closes the doubled contradiction. The exact preceding 11.2.1
alternative then yields k≤n for the original invariant flag, with its actual
outside-component consumer. The completed generation theorem now supplies
that alternative without an odd-kernel or native-cover premise. `Complete`
combines the exclusion with the earlier lower bound to prove k=n and applies
it to the literal residual component. RankOneReduction and the earlier
lower bound remain explicit with qt-d-1222-shadow-parameter-component;
their discharge is independent of this completed doubled-source implication.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 11.3.6, printed pp.772--773.
-/
